    "body": "The retained session now has a seven-slot ternary recurrent lexical component that learns variable preludes and termination around owned copied spans. The principal review retains its 31/31 exposed authored outputs while correcting the interpretation, comparator, snapshot validation and prospective training objective.\n\nThe submitted finite reference was trained on the wrong emission-count/history observations. Its corrected replay is12/31; the unchanged learned artifact remains31/31, with322/322 historical teacher-forced steps. All124 nonreference rows retain original bytes and terminals. This is a useful recurrent component, not a completed transferable language model: copied tokens share one feedback symbol, content is truncated/orderless and skips unknowns, all computed contrasts are fitted, and self-valued route fixtures do not establish temporal mutation semantics. E/S comparison and ordinary-text learning remain unexecuted.\n\nCorrectness repairs bind recurrent state and owned operands during restore, validate arithmetic bounds, align rounded QAT biases and objective normalization, and compare full parent/child effects and final sessions. Original models and all sealed results are preserved; trainer repairs do not retroactively change historical fitting evidence.\n\nValidation executed locally:46 distinct focused library tests including7 new tests; release runner build; unchanged-artifact exposed replay in a new sealed25-file root;10 parent and10 separate-process full continuation comparisons; independently recomputed source/result/seal audit; cargo fmt, claim wording and diff checks. Full suite and whole-path D0-b/energy qualification were not run. CI compatibility names are acknowledgements, not these test results.\n\nThe canonical plan, current state, README, evidence, resource ledger, principal review and comprehensive DeepSeek brief now keep the next milestone at one transferable lexical learner: exact observed semantics, real copied/generated-token feedback, post-copy continuation, source-separated ordinary text, a loaded E/S reference and full-candidate retention. Geometry remains preferred through structured ordered transport/shared residual candidates with competent comparisons. Broad prose and executed Rust follow useful lexical progress.\n\nReferences #820, #973, #1139, #962, #963, #964.\n",
